        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0590" n="490" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg490"/>

                <head>No. 355.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Reed to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-04-08"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 8, 1884</date>.
                        (Received April 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 247.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Foster’s No. 199 in regard
                    to passports in the Island of Cuba, I have now the honor to inclose herewith,
                    for your further information, a copy and translation of a note dated the 3d
                    instant, from the Minister of State, stating that the subject has been referred
                    to the Minister of Ultramar, whose reply thereto will be sent to this legation
                    as soon as received.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DWIGHT F. REED.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d355-a1.xml" xpointer="d355-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
